WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.767 --> 00:00:01.767
-Welcome back.

00:00:01.767 --> 00:00:03.067
We're hanging out
with Amy Schumer,

00:00:03.067 --> 00:00:04.367
ladies and gentlemen, now.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:04.367 --> 00:00:06.133
-Oh. Stop.
Wow.

00:00:06.133 --> 00:00:08.033
-Amy...
-Wow. I'm very humble.

00:00:08.033 --> 00:00:10.200
-Amy I wanted to mention --
I know.

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:11.467
You said that.
-Very, very humble.

00:00:11.467 --> 00:00:12.501
-I know.

00:00:12.501 --> 00:00:13.701
-It's one of the best things
about me.

00:00:13.701 --> 00:00:14.901
-I know.
-Yeah.

00:00:14.901 --> 00:00:16.501
-I did want to mention --
this is a big deal --

00:00:16.501 --> 00:00:18.300
you are going
to host the Oscars this year.

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:20.367
-Oh, my God. I am?
-This is a giant deal, yeah.

00:00:20.367 --> 00:00:21.834
-This is big.
-Congratulations.

00:00:21.834 --> 00:00:23.501
-Me and Regina Hall
and Wanda Sykes.

00:00:23.501 --> 00:00:24.801
[ Cheers and applause ]
That's right.

00:00:24.801 --> 00:00:27.667
-Regina Hall and Wanda Sykes.

00:00:27.667 --> 00:00:30.100
How did it come about?
Did you immediately say yes?

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:32.100
Like, "This is great.
I'm in," or...?

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:33.934
-Yeah. I was --

00:00:33.934 --> 00:00:36.000
I mean, I just feel like
performing right now.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:38.000
Coming out of the pandemic
and everything,

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:39.100
you know, hopefully --
-Yes.

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:41.534
[ Knocks on wood ]

00:00:41.534 --> 00:00:43.267
-I just feel
really excited about it.

00:00:43.267 --> 00:00:45.501
I want to go and, you know,
get into some trouble.

00:00:45.501 --> 00:00:46.534
-Yeah!
-You know?

00:00:46.534 --> 00:00:47.901
-We need trouble.
We need fun.

00:00:47.901 --> 00:00:49.434
We need some entertainment.
-Let's go.

00:00:49.434 --> 00:00:50.868
-Congratulations.
-Thank you.

00:00:50.868 --> 00:00:51.901
-And it's gonna be great, bud.

00:00:51.901 --> 00:00:54.133
I want to talk about
"Life &amp; Beth."

00:00:54.133 --> 00:00:55.434
-Yes.
-We just had Jon Glaser

00:00:55.434 --> 00:00:56.968
on the show --
-Oh, I'm sorry.

00:00:56.968 --> 00:00:58.033
[ Laughter ]
-No, no!

00:00:58.033 --> 00:00:59.100
I was gonna say
he was fantastic.

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:01.367
-Oh, good!
Oh, good, yeah.

00:01:01.367 --> 00:01:02.901
-Gosh, you have a great cast.

00:01:02.901 --> 00:01:04.701
-It's ridiculous.
-It is insane.

00:01:04.701 --> 00:01:06.200
-It's too much.
-No, it's great.

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:08.133
-I wish I caught their names
while they were there, but...

00:01:08.133 --> 00:01:09.334
[ Laughter ]

00:01:09.334 --> 00:01:11.334
-They're a really great cast.
"Life &amp; Beth."

00:01:11.334 --> 00:01:13.834
But this came about because,
during the pandemic,

00:01:13.834 --> 00:01:15.601
you were looking through old,
like, diaries?

00:01:15.601 --> 00:01:16.701
What is...?
-Yeah, I mean,

00:01:16.701 --> 00:01:18.601
I got weird over the pandemic.

00:01:18.601 --> 00:01:19.734
-I think we all did
a little bit.

00:01:19.734 --> 00:01:22.100
-You know, yeah,
just in dark, dark places.

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:25.634
And I was just looking back
at my journals

00:01:25.634 --> 00:01:27.734
and, like, sort of
the teenage traumas.

00:01:27.734 --> 00:01:29.400
And I'm also, like,
a new mom,

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:32.400
and I'm learning that
all toddlers want is empathy.

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:35.067
And surprise, surprise,
that's all adults want, also.

00:01:35.067 --> 00:01:36.667
-Yeah. Exactly, right?
-You know?

00:01:36.667 --> 00:01:39.467
So, I just thought
it's really important to,

00:01:39.467 --> 00:01:43.300
you know, kind of confront
those traumas, and --

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:45.000
in order to move forward.
-Yeah.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:47.067
-So, I wanted
to make a show about that.

00:01:47.067 --> 00:01:48.234
And, uh...
-And you did.

00:01:48.234 --> 00:01:51.267
-And somebody said I could,
so I did.

00:01:51.267 --> 00:01:52.467
-Do you want to explain
your character

00:01:52.467 --> 00:01:53.901
and who you play in the show?

00:01:53.901 --> 00:01:56.334
-Yes, I am a supermodel --

00:01:56.334 --> 00:01:58.000
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:00.968
-I'm a runway model -- no.
Beth is --

00:02:00.968 --> 00:02:04.167
I play a woman who works in --
Everything looks really good.

00:02:04.167 --> 00:02:06.901
She has a hot boyfriend,
living in Manhattan,

00:02:06.901 --> 00:02:09.033
has a cool job
working with wine.

00:02:09.033 --> 00:02:11.167
-Yeah.
-But she's miserable.

00:02:11.167 --> 00:02:13.267
You know, like,
all these things she thought

00:02:13.267 --> 00:02:14.534
that would make her happy
aren't.

00:02:14.534 --> 00:02:15.901
-Aren't making her happy.
-Right.

00:02:15.901 --> 00:02:17.400
-It's very, very funny.
You guys are gonna enjoy this.

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:19.300
I want to show everyone a clip.
Here's Amy Schumer

00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:22.000
in the new show "Life &amp; Beth."
Take a look at this.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:23.534
♪♪

00:02:23.534 --> 00:02:27.133
-Plan A didn't work out?

00:02:27.133 --> 00:02:28.834
-Shut up.

00:02:28.834 --> 00:02:31.534
-You must be...Matt?

00:02:31.534 --> 00:02:32.834
-Are you in here a lot?

00:02:32.834 --> 00:02:35.534
-This is not Matt, okay?

00:02:35.534 --> 00:02:38.667
This is Trevor.
-Travis.

00:02:38.667 --> 00:02:40.033
-Travis.

00:02:40.033 --> 00:02:42.033
-Here. You wanna
just take that now?

00:02:43.667 --> 00:02:44.901
-Excuse me?

00:02:44.901 --> 00:02:47.067
-Oh, damn.

00:02:47.067 --> 00:02:48.601
[ Laughter and applause ]
-Yeah, that's exactly right.

00:02:48.601 --> 00:02:50.200
Amy Schumer, everybody!

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:54.801
All episodes of "Life &amp; Beth"
will be on Hulu this Friday!

